o reduce skewness in distribution of distance-related features.\n# Usefulness: Rescales highly skewed numerical features, improving prediction performance and algorithm stability.\ndf['Log_Fire_Distance'] = np.log(df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points'] + 1)  # Adding 1 to avoid log(0)", "# Log_Road_Distance\n# Feature description: Log transformation of Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways to reduce skewness in distribution of distance-related features.\n# Usefulness: Encodes a more normalized representation of road proximity, aiding models sensitive to feature distributions.\ndf['Log_Road_Distance'] = np.log(df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways'] + 1)", "# Amenities_Proximity\n# Feature description: Ratio-based feature combining horizontal distances to hydrology, fire points, and roadways.\n# Usefulness: Highlights the relative importance of proximity to various features in shaping forest cover type.\ndf['Amenities_Proximity'] = df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Hydrology'] / (df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points'] + df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways'] + 1)", "# Slope_Binned\n# Feature description: Binning Slope into categorical ranges (Flat <10°, Moderate 10-30°, Steep ≥30°).\n# Usefulness: Captures non-linear relationships between terrain steepness and forest cover type while simplifying data complexity.\ndf['Slope_Binned'] = pd.cut(df['Slope'], bins=[0, 10, 30, 66], labels=['Flat', 'Moderate', 'Steep'], include_lowest=True)", "# Hillshade_Ratio\n# Feature description: Ratio of morning Hillshade (Hillshade_9am) to afternoon Hillshade (Hillshade_3pm).\n# Usefulness: Models the overall gradient in sunlight exposure over the terrain throughout a day, key for forest type differentiation.\ndf['Hillshade_Ratio'] = df['Hillshade_9am'] / (df['Hillshade_3pm'] + 1)", "# Wilderness_Encoded\n# Feature description: Combines Wilderness_Area1 through Wilderness_Area4 into a single categorical feature using label encoding.\n# Usefulness: Reduces dimensionality of sparse wilderness indicators while preserving semantic structure of wilderness classifications.\ndf['Wilderness_Encoded'] = df[['Wilderness_Area1', 'Wilderness_Area2', 'Wilderness_Area3', 'Wilderness_Area4']].idxmax(axis=1)\ndf['Wilderness_Encoded'] = df['Wilderness_Encoded'].str.extract('Wilderness_Area(\\d)').astype(int)", "df.drop(columns=['Vegetation_Zones', 'Slope_Steepness_Category', 'Wilderness_Area1', 'Wilderness_Area2', 'Wilderness_Area3', 'Wilderness_Area4'], inplace=True)"]
